{"name":"Inca Gold","hex":"#aa6d28","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"inca","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several species of hummingbirds in the genus Coeligena"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inca"},{"term":"gold","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy yellow elemental metal of great value, with atomic number 79.","A coin or coinage made of this material, or supposedly so."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["☉ (alchemy)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gold"}],"entries":[{"title":"Inca Empire","blocks":[{"text":"The Inca Empire, officially known as the Realm of the Four Parts, was the largest empire in pre-Columbian America. The administrative, political, and military center of the empire was in the city of Cusco. The Inca civilisation rose from the Peruvian highlands sometime in the early 13th century. The Portuguese explorer Aleixo Garcia was the first European to reach the Inca Empire in 1524. Later, in 1532, the Spanish began the conquest of the Inca Empire, and by 1572 the last Inca state was fully conquered."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Banner_of_the_Inca_Empire.svg/330px-Banner_of_the_Inca_Empire.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inca_Empire","wikidata":"Q28573"},{"title":"Gold","blocks":[{"text":"Gold is a chemical element; its chemical symbol is Au and atomic number 79. In its pure form, it is a bright-metallic-yellow, dense, soft, malleable, and ductile metal. Chemically, gold is a transition metal, a group 11 element, and one of the noble metals. It is one of the least reactive chemical elements, being the second lowest in the reactivity series, with only platinum ranked as less reactive. Gold is solid under standard conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Gold-crystals.jpg/330px-Gold-crystals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold","wikidata":"Q897"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Machu_Picchu_Panorama_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Machu_Picchu_Panorama_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Machu_Picchu_Panorama_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Machu_Picchu_Panorama_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Machu_Picchu_Panorama_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Machu_Picchu_Panorama_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMachu_Picchu_Panorama_2025_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Tiwanaku1.jpg/500px-Tiwanaku1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Tiwanaku1.jpg/500px-Tiwanaku1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stela in Tiwanaku's Kalasasaya temple","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATiwanaku1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Brooklyn_Museum_-_Manco_Capac%2C_First_Inca%2C_1_of_14_Portraits_of_Inca_Kings_-_overall.jpg/500px-Brooklyn_Museum_-_Manco_Capac%2C_First_Inca%2C_1_of_14_Portraits_of